{{userbox
| id-c = {{{{{1|any}}}-color|light}}
| info-c = {{{{{1|any}}}-color|lighter}}
| id = [[Image:{{{2|Churning Earth}}}.png|45px]]
| info = [[{{{2|Churning Earth}}}]] is {{{3|this user}}}'s favorite {{#switch:{{{4|}}}|yes|y|elite|e=elite|#default=}} skill.
}}<noinclude>__NOTOC__{{clear}}
== Usage ==
<pre>{{User favorite skill|1|2|3|4}}</pre>

=== Parameters ===
1: Profession: In the form "<code>e</code>", "<code>w</code>", "<code>g</code>", etc. This gives the template the color information.<br/>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; If it's a common skill, you can either omit this parameter or chose "<code>any</code>".<br>
2: Skill name: In the form seen on the wiki or in-game, i.e. "<code>Churning Earth</code>".<br>
3: Your name, your character's name:  This will show up as "[...] is <code>Elementalist</code> favorite skill." Defaults to "this user".<br>
4: Elite status: State with "<code>yes</code>", "<code>y</code>", "<code>elite</code>" or "<code>e</code>" that you skill is elite to include this in the box description.

== Example ==
<pre>{{User favorite skill|e|Mist Form|Example|yes}}</pre>

{{User favorite skill|e|Mist Form|Example|yes}}
